    "secondary": "max_absolute_deviation_percentage_points",
    "why": "the three risk levels are the only commensurable coordinates between the two designs, RMSE weights them equally, penalises a single badly missed condition more than a mean absolute error would, and reports in the same percentage-point units the manuscript's tables use; the Chebyshev distance is reported beside it so one bad condition stays visible"
